H. Assumption Challenge
  Considered vertices: runners, gaps, fixed circle sections, section
  boundaries, wall-crossing events, residues, cover arcs, Fourier modes,
  Haar rectangles, centered edge signs, endpoint owners, incident cores,
  survivor gates, and proof obligations.
  Chosen quotient: color-packet proof obligations.  It preserves AP-tail
  gate availability, floor count, endpoint phase, and sidecar debt
  declaration, but destroys raw runner identity, non-AP geometry, and
  arbitrary primitive-row adjacency.  Challenged assumption: a coloring
  quotient is harmless if its classes look balanced.  The audit shows
  balance is insufficient unless floor, endpoint, branch, and zeta colors
  remain reconstructible.
